WEBVTT

00:01:45.100 --> 00:01:46.940
BROKEN FISH TANKS

00:02:20.800 --> 00:02:24.220
I never had any thoughts of my own.

00:02:25.350 --> 00:02:27.430
Not until Tsukasa turned up.

00:02:50.920 --> 00:02:53.210
I wanted to stay inside

00:02:53.500 --> 00:02:55.960
that beautiful water forever.

00:02:59.130 --> 00:03:01.970
That's why I chose to become a goldfish.

00:03:02.470 --> 00:03:05.220
No! Make the whole pan yellow!

00:03:05.430 --> 00:03:06.600
What?

00:03:06.810 --> 00:03:08.980
It's not all yellow yet!

00:03:09.230 --> 00:03:11.480
You want me to fill
the whole pan with batter?

00:03:11.690 --> 00:03:13.440
That's not how you make pancakes.

00:03:16.610 --> 00:03:17.940
Hiroki!

00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:21.200
I made the whole pan yellow today!

00:03:21.530 --> 00:03:24.450
That's amazing, Tsukasa!

00:03:26.200 --> 00:03:29.750
Nobody knows Tsukasa like I do.

00:03:30.210 --> 00:03:34.000
There's no way he would crush
his own peak giver!

00:03:34.920 --> 00:03:38.590
So why did it look the same
as Tsukasa's peak did?

00:03:39.670 --> 00:03:43.010
I think this is my first time
 in a car with you, Mr. Hayashi.

00:03:43.640 --> 00:03:46.260
It was Hayashi who Tsukasa fought.

00:03:46.680 --> 00:03:50.270
And he's Tsukasa's peak giver,
as well as Satoru's.

00:03:50.770 --> 00:03:52.270
I can't let myself think about it.

00:03:53.350 --> 00:03:56.310
I didn't let myself
think about stuff either.

00:03:56.570 --> 00:03:59.900
I always ignored it when Tsukasa
kept things secret from me.

00:04:00.690 --> 00:04:02.900
Because I wanted to trust him.

00:04:03.570 --> 00:04:04.570
Hiroki...

00:04:05.530 --> 00:04:09.160
What is a "pet", Tsukasa?

00:04:11.370 --> 00:04:14.920
Hayashi said I was a "pet"!

00:04:18.550 --> 00:04:20.210
W...What?

00:04:20.710 --> 00:04:21.760
Tsukasa...?

00:04:22.880 --> 00:04:25.430
Mr. Hayashi's alive then?!

00:04:25.680 --> 00:04:27.300
You saw him, didn't you!

00:04:27.510 --> 00:04:28.930
Where is he?

00:04:29.390 --> 00:04:31.930
You didn't crush him...?

00:04:33.390 --> 00:04:34.310
Tsukasa?

00:04:34.900 --> 00:04:36.440
But you just said...

00:04:36.810 --> 00:04:39.020
you spoke to him, right?

00:04:39.320 --> 00:04:40.440
That's not what I said!

00:04:40.650 --> 00:04:44.450
I went into his memories,
at the hospital.

00:04:45.030 --> 00:04:46.660
There was a wind blowing,

00:04:46.870 --> 00:04:49.700
and it led me to him lying there
like he'd been crushed.

00:04:50.290 --> 00:04:52.700
So, I synced up with him

00:04:52.910 --> 00:04:54.870
like I did with you that time...

00:04:55.330 --> 00:04:58.210
But when I got there,
his memories were all jumbled up.

00:04:59.130 --> 00:05:02.420
And in the end his peak disappeared,
even the wind itself...

00:05:03.260 --> 00:05:05.760
He was crushed and it all vanished.

00:05:07.800 --> 00:05:08.720
Tsukasa...?

00:05:11.720 --> 00:05:14.350
-Tsukasa?
-There's a bug in the cash register.

00:05:15.810 --> 00:05:18.020
Forget that, I wanna know...

00:05:18.520 --> 00:05:21.360
Let's speak in the tank,
like last time, okay?

00:05:23.280 --> 00:05:23.990
No.

00:05:24.490 --> 00:05:26.740
Tell me what "pet" means first, Tsukasa.

00:05:27.490 --> 00:05:29.870
I've had enough of
being kept in the dark!

00:05:34.500 --> 00:05:36.870
A new pet for Mr. Hayashi?

00:05:37.420 --> 00:05:40.000
He already has Satoru.
Why a new one?

00:05:40.340 --> 00:05:44.130
Because your pet
is causing problems, Tsukasa.

00:05:44.340 --> 00:05:46.630
He's constantly defying Company orders.

00:05:47.180 --> 00:05:52.100
Could Mr. Hayashi not talk to Hiroki
and explain things?

00:05:52.470 --> 00:05:55.430
If Hiroki understood that my peak giver
is also an employee...

00:05:55.730 --> 00:05:57.020
There you go again!

00:05:57.190 --> 00:06:01.400
Are you training your pet badly on purpose
as a way to try and see Hayashi?

00:06:02.940 --> 00:06:05.990
Increasing the numbers like this
is too much of a risk.

00:06:06.190 --> 00:06:08.660
There has to be a better way
to create pets.

00:06:08.990 --> 00:06:10.910
We could make pets that don't have locks.

00:06:11.120 --> 00:06:14.370
If we did, Mr. Hayashi wouldn't have
to be constantly minding them.

00:06:14.580 --> 00:06:18.160
Wouldn't a pet without a lock
be pretty useless to us...?

00:06:18.420 --> 00:06:20.920
To pets, not having a lock means

00:06:21.130 --> 00:06:22.920
they can only have a peak.

00:06:23.460 --> 00:06:26.550
You guys are different to us
in that you specialize in crushing.

00:06:27.220 --> 00:06:31.430
Since you don't use images, you can only
sync to loci with strong memories.

00:06:32.050 --> 00:06:34.140
But if a pet with only a peak
was with you,

00:06:34.430 --> 00:06:38.270
you'd be able to sync up to that pet
and use their image.

00:06:38.520 --> 00:06:42.730
In effect, you could use them to guide you
through a target's memories.

00:06:42.940 --> 00:06:47.570
That should then enable you
to manipulate those memories.

00:06:48.030 --> 00:06:53.240
A pet that's loyal to the Company and
doesn't bite the hand that feeds it, eh?

00:06:55.370 --> 00:06:58.580
The Company only started calling us "pets"

00:06:58.790 --> 00:07:04.840
when Long decided to poke fun at
Mr. Hayashi for keeping me at his side.

00:07:06.880 --> 00:07:10.720
But Mr. Hayashi is the one who
we should be worrying about now.

00:07:11.840 --> 00:07:15.220
Why do you think the Company is keeping
him alive after he was crushed?

00:07:16.140 --> 00:07:20.230
It's so they can prove to Satoru that
I was the one who crushed him.

00:07:21.480 --> 00:07:25.730
The damn CEO has thought up
a very persuasive performance.

00:07:25.940 --> 00:07:27.400
He knows full well

00:07:27.610 --> 00:07:32.610
that we yearn to be with our peak givers
so intensely it's like a curse.

00:07:32.990 --> 00:07:38.160
And now he's planning on using Satoru
to make me do as he wishes.

00:07:38.450 --> 00:07:42.330
So we're going to crush Satoru
before that happens!

00:07:43.460 --> 00:07:47.000
What are you talking about, Tsukasa?

00:07:47.710 --> 00:07:50.470
Why do we need to crush Satoru?

00:07:50.670 --> 00:07:51.630
Listen.

00:07:51.800 --> 00:07:56.390
If Satoru knew that I'd crushed Hayashi,
his peak giver, he'd become our enemy.

00:07:56.680 --> 00:07:59.640
-We have to act first...
-What're you talking about?!

00:07:59.850 --> 00:08:04.020
Hayashi or whatever his name is,
he's your peak giver too, right?

00:08:04.310 --> 00:08:10.030
The thing I can't understand most of all
is why you crushed your own peak giver!

00:08:10.240 --> 00:08:12.150
Why the hell did you do it, Tsukasa?

00:08:13.820 --> 00:08:17.330
Mr. Hayashi didn't like my methods...

00:08:17.530 --> 00:08:18.580
What methods?

00:08:18.790 --> 00:08:22.660
The memory you saw.
The idea of having pets without locks.

00:08:23.120 --> 00:08:25.040
The Company calls them "babies".

00:08:25.250 --> 00:08:27.540
I don't like it either, you know!

00:08:27.880 --> 00:08:30.880
Who can live properly without a lock?

00:08:31.130 --> 00:08:35.180
It's not your problem.
No one's asking you to make a "baby".

00:08:35.510 --> 00:08:36.680
It is my problem!

00:08:37.140 --> 00:08:41.520
So you're saying you crushed Hayashi
because he didn't agree with you?

00:08:41.730 --> 00:08:42.930
That's not it!

00:08:43.180 --> 00:08:47.190
Mr. Hayashi ran away!
He betrayed the Company!

00:08:47.690 --> 00:08:48.980
I don't believe it...

00:08:49.230 --> 00:08:51.190
You crushed him just for that?

00:08:51.530 --> 00:08:52.990
"Just for that"...?

00:08:53.150 --> 00:08:55.700
If you're saying he was a traitor
who had to be crushed,

00:08:56.200 --> 00:08:59.830
then you'll have to do
the same thing to me!

00:09:00.080 --> 00:09:01.580
What are you saying Hiroki?

00:09:01.950 --> 00:09:04.040
Why would I do such a thing...?

00:09:04.330 --> 00:09:07.710
Because I don't want to be told
what to do by the Company either!

00:09:08.040 --> 00:09:11.630
I'm just going along with it all
to be with you, Tsukasa!

00:09:11.840 --> 00:09:13.300
The same goes for me.

00:09:13.510 --> 00:09:16.220
I'm doing all of this
so we can live together freely.

00:09:16.510 --> 00:09:17.340
Well, then...

00:09:17.720 --> 00:09:22.140
But the Company wants
to take you away from me!

00:09:22.390 --> 00:09:26.350
If I don't let them, they'll reveal
to Satoru that I crushed Hayashi!

00:09:27.350 --> 00:09:31.360
So, there's no other way
but to crush Satoru.

00:09:34.940 --> 00:09:36.700
We can run away, Tsukasa.

00:09:38.280 --> 00:09:41.530
If we're really at a stage where
our only choice is to crush Satoru,

00:09:41.700 --> 00:09:44.250
then let's run away
from this shitty company!

00:09:44.620 --> 00:09:45.410
Run away?

00:09:45.580 --> 00:09:48.370
Yes... we can make it if we're together.

00:09:48.790 --> 00:09:52.920
Why would I do...
the same thing Mr. Hayashi did?

00:09:53.210 --> 00:09:54.260
Why...?

00:09:54.760 --> 00:09:58.510
The real question is why you'd work
for a company whose rules you can't stand.

00:09:59.140 --> 00:10:02.390
If we can just run away, what was it for?

00:10:02.890 --> 00:10:04.520
I crushed...

00:10:04.680 --> 00:10:07.100
I crushed Mr. Hayashi because he ran.

00:10:07.730 --> 00:10:10.190
If we could just make a run for it,

00:10:10.560 --> 00:10:12.650
why would I have crushed Mr. Hayashi?

00:10:12.860 --> 00:10:15.490
Why... would... I?

00:10:16.950 --> 00:10:18.910
Tsukasa, you must've got things wrong.

00:10:19.490 --> 00:10:22.530
I can't believe you'd crush
your peak giver.

00:10:22.740 --> 00:10:24.330
You're wrong.

00:10:24.700 --> 00:10:26.080
I mean...

00:10:26.580 --> 00:10:29.040
I'm not wrong, Hiroki.

00:10:29.500 --> 00:10:32.460
Just because the Company wanted you to,
you wouldn't...

00:10:33.500 --> 00:10:37.420
I'm not wrong! I'm not wrong, you hear!

00:10:37.970 --> 00:10:39.800
Don't contradict me!

00:10:40.300 --> 00:10:41.260
Tsukasa...

00:10:41.550 --> 00:10:42.720
I understand, Hiroki.

00:10:42.970 --> 00:10:46.520
I know you're saying those things because
you don't want Satoru to be crushed.

00:10:46.890 --> 00:10:49.810
In that case, I'll just erase Satoru
from your memory.

00:10:50.600 --> 00:10:53.310
It'll be easy to crush him
if he's just a random guy, right?

00:10:53.820 --> 00:10:55.020
Hiroki...

00:10:55.230 --> 00:10:59.070
let's go to your peak. I can erase
your memory of Satoru from there.

00:11:00.070 --> 00:11:02.370
I don't want to, Tsukasa!

00:11:08.370 --> 00:11:09.370
Hiroki...

00:11:11.210 --> 00:11:12.210
No...

00:11:12.420 --> 00:11:13.380
Hiroki.

00:11:13.590 --> 00:11:14.380
I don't want to!

00:11:15.000 --> 00:11:15.800
Hiroki!

00:11:18.090 --> 00:11:20.800
Hiroki, open the door. Hiroki!

00:11:20.970 --> 00:11:22.840
Open this door!

00:11:28.430 --> 00:11:30.600
Hiroki ran out of the shop! Grab him!

00:11:30.850 --> 00:11:31.850
Don't lose him!

00:11:34.650 --> 00:11:35.770
Hiroki!

00:11:36.860 --> 00:11:39.690
Where are you going?
You're going to leave me behind...?

00:11:40.190 --> 00:11:41.200
But...

00:11:41.700 --> 00:11:43.700
I'll go with you, Hiroki...

00:11:44.320 --> 00:11:45.330
Tsukasa...?

00:11:45.580 --> 00:11:47.410
Stay there. I'll come out.

00:11:51.920 --> 00:11:52.790
Crap!

00:11:53.120 --> 00:11:54.420
You can't escape, you know!

00:11:54.580 --> 00:11:57.420
After him! Don't let him get away!

00:12:10.180 --> 00:12:11.180
You can't move.

00:12:12.690 --> 00:12:13.730
Go to sleep.

00:12:19.030 --> 00:12:21.610
Why, Tsukasa?

00:12:27.490 --> 00:12:30.870
Don't you think we should
widen the search area?

00:12:32.500 --> 00:12:35.790
Tokyo's a pretty big place, after all.

00:12:36.250 --> 00:12:39.130
Hiroki will be nearby. I just know it!

00:12:39.300 --> 00:12:42.630
He ran off in the heat of the moment
and will be regretting it already.

00:12:43.010 --> 00:12:45.970
Dammit! He's completely vulnerable
on his own!

00:12:46.760 --> 00:12:49.680
Do you think he'll be back when
his belly needs filling?

00:12:51.680 --> 00:12:53.940
Don't you get it, Katsuragi?

00:12:54.310 --> 00:12:57.900
Fish can't live outside of water.

00:12:59.610 --> 00:13:02.740
Hiroki saw Hayashi after
he'd nearly been crushed?

00:13:03.610 --> 00:13:05.780
Right. Then he found out

00:13:06.160 --> 00:13:09.870
that Tsukasa was the one who
crushed him, and flew the coop.

00:13:11.080 --> 00:13:13.620
But, Hayashi...

00:13:14.290 --> 00:13:16.460
Oh, so he's alive?

00:13:16.750 --> 00:13:17.880
No problem.

00:13:18.960 --> 00:13:20.130
Tsukasa?

00:13:24.760 --> 00:13:25.550
Tsukasa.

00:13:26.050 --> 00:13:27.050
You found him?

00:13:27.640 --> 00:13:29.350
Nope. But Mr. Long is on the phone...

00:13:30.640 --> 00:13:31.930
You lied, you bastard!

00:13:32.100 --> 00:13:34.390
I thought you'd taken care of Hayashi?

00:13:34.600 --> 00:13:40.570
I assumed that's what you wanted to hear,
given how much you hated him.

00:13:40.730 --> 00:13:45.110
But despite appearances,
we're actually old buddies, me and him.

00:13:45.650 --> 00:13:48.110
You understand that, right?

00:13:48.990 --> 00:13:53.080
If you'd just let me dive into
Hayashi after he was crushed,

00:13:53.290 --> 00:13:54.750
this would never have happened.

00:13:55.200 --> 00:13:59.670
More importantly, how did Hiroki
know where to find Hayashi?

00:13:59.920 --> 00:14:03.000
He was lured there by Hayashi's image.

00:14:03.550 --> 00:14:05.550
His lock's so weak,

00:14:05.720 --> 00:14:08.380
he could see Hayashi's image leaking out.

00:14:09.010 --> 00:14:10.090
So...

00:14:11.550 --> 00:14:14.390
Wait a minute... His lock...

00:14:14.890 --> 00:14:17.350
His lock is broken
so the contents seep out.

00:14:17.560 --> 00:14:19.400
-That means...
-What?

00:14:19.900 --> 00:14:23.400
Please tell Long to come
to Japan with Meiling!

00:14:23.610 --> 00:14:25.400
We'll soon find Hiroki!

00:14:25.570 --> 00:14:27.700
That's right, Meiling!

00:14:27.860 --> 00:14:30.160
Meiling will be able to locate him!

00:14:33.700 --> 00:14:37.120
Well, look at that. The light stretches

00:14:37.290 --> 00:14:39.920
if you squint at it.

00:14:40.630 --> 00:14:43.880
Oh, Mr. Long. How are you keeping?

00:14:44.130 --> 00:14:48.050
If you're after Tsukasa, he's checking
the wiretap recordings at the pizza place.

00:14:48.380 --> 00:14:50.050
What the hell happened here?

00:14:51.470 --> 00:14:54.680
Tsukasa went nuts and smashed everything.

00:14:55.140 --> 00:14:57.060
You think this is a laughing matter?

00:14:57.230 --> 00:14:59.940
Isn't your negligence
the root cause of all this?

00:15:00.310 --> 00:15:04.440
Why did Hiroki even see Hayashi
while he was on your watch?

00:15:05.610 --> 00:15:09.320
I'd be careful if I were you. Screw up
too often and you'll get rubbed out.

00:15:10.450 --> 00:15:13.620
The CEO won't do anything to me.

00:15:13.830 --> 00:15:17.450
He's given me his word that
I won't be killed.

00:15:18.120 --> 00:15:19.040
Huh.

00:15:19.500 --> 00:15:22.210
You gotta be kidding me...

00:15:22.830 --> 00:15:24.000
It may not look like it,

00:15:24.290 --> 00:15:27.300
but I quite like that Katsuragi.

00:15:27.630 --> 00:15:33.010
I guess his incompetence is only surpassed
by his loyalty to the Company.

00:15:33.680 --> 00:15:38.100
Truth is, Katsuragi's had his memories
manipulated by Hayashi.

00:15:39.100 --> 00:15:41.600
I had no idea. When did that happen?

00:15:41.810 --> 00:15:44.730
Soon after my father was killed.

00:15:45.230 --> 00:15:47.570
Katsuragi has unwavering faith in me.

00:15:47.780 --> 00:15:51.700
You couldn't ask for a more easily led
"perfect employee".

00:15:51.860 --> 00:15:53.450
I'll tell you what else.

00:15:53.740 --> 00:15:57.540
Ever since Hayashi manipulated
Katsuragi's memories,

00:15:57.790 --> 00:16:02.540
I've been waiting for the chance
to get my hands on a "perfect pet".

00:16:02.790 --> 00:16:07.500
That's why I made use of
their intimate bonds the way I did.

00:16:08.880 --> 00:16:11.050
You brought Meiling with you, right?

00:16:11.260 --> 00:16:13.130
She's over there.

00:16:15.140 --> 00:16:17.760
Meiling will be sure to find Hiroki.

00:16:18.100 --> 00:16:23.230
Hiroki managed to catch Hayashi's image
from afar, before he was crushed,

00:16:23.440 --> 00:16:27.440
because Hayashi's lock was broken
and his image was leaking out.

00:16:27.860 --> 00:16:31.530
If I'm right, Meiling is in
the same state Hayashi was in.

00:16:31.990 --> 00:16:35.660
She doesn't have a lock,
so her image must also be leaking out.

00:16:36.740 --> 00:16:40.790
In other words, Meiling's image is
active outside her body

00:16:40.950 --> 00:16:43.040
even when she isn't using it for work.

00:16:43.750 --> 00:16:46.290
Her butterfly is probably
fluttering about right now

00:16:46.500 --> 00:16:50.420
waiting for somebody to sync up with it.

00:16:50.840 --> 00:16:54.800
And Hiroki might be
the one person who can see it!

00:16:56.140 --> 00:16:58.260
Seeing as they're both image users,

00:16:58.430 --> 00:17:01.430
and Hiroki's lock is also weak,
he can sense her butterfly!

00:17:01.970 --> 00:17:04.310
You know what this means, Long?

00:17:04.560 --> 00:17:07.860
We can sync up to anyone
who can see Meiling's butterfly!

00:17:08.060 --> 00:17:11.480
My point is, we only need Hiroki
to spot that butterfly,

00:17:11.690 --> 00:17:15.200
and we can sync up to him
even if he's far away.

00:17:16.030 --> 00:17:17.950
And then what?

00:17:18.320 --> 00:17:21.040
If I can just sync up to Hiroki
with Meiling,

00:17:21.540 --> 00:17:25.460
I can search his memories
and find out where he's hiding!

00:17:25.670 --> 00:17:28.130
And I can persuade him to come back!

00:17:28.540 --> 00:17:31.210
There's no need
to persuade him to do anything.

00:17:31.880 --> 00:17:35.720
Our orders are to find Hiroki
and then kill him.

00:17:38.050 --> 00:17:39.970
Why would you need to kill him?!

00:17:40.180 --> 00:17:43.980
He just ran out in a huff, that's all!
If I could just speak to him...

00:17:44.310 --> 00:17:45.480
You think he'll listen to you?

00:17:45.640 --> 00:17:47.690
He knows you crushed your peak giver

00:17:47.900 --> 00:17:50.360
and has lost all trust in you, remember?

00:17:50.770 --> 00:17:52.730
This is a "pet" we've lost, got it?

00:17:53.150 --> 00:17:56.740
It might be you who ends up
getting persuaded by him!

00:17:57.150 --> 00:18:00.780
Did you really think the CEO
was going to let a pet like that live?

00:18:00.990 --> 00:18:05.250
That bromance you had with your pet
has come back to bite you on the ass!

00:18:08.750 --> 00:18:11.250
Your job here is done.

00:18:11.750 --> 00:18:16.130
Now that we know how to find him,
Meiling and I will take care of it.

00:18:16.970 --> 00:18:18.720
You don't have to kill him.

00:18:18.880 --> 00:18:21.140
Do we have a problem here?

00:18:21.510 --> 00:18:22.810
I don't mean it like that.

00:18:23.010 --> 00:18:26.270
If you're going to kill him, we might
as well try to change his memories.

00:18:26.890 --> 00:18:29.270
Change them so he complies
with the Company's orders.

00:18:29.730 --> 00:18:33.520
We could make him think
his peak giver is the CEO.

00:18:36.240 --> 00:18:40.030
That's impossible. You'd need
some crazy scheme to pull that off.

00:18:40.450 --> 00:18:44.410
The scheme just needs Satoru.
With him onboard we'd have the upper hand.

00:18:44.740 --> 00:18:46.330
Satoru?

00:18:46.540 --> 00:18:49.040
And what if he finds out
you crushed Hayashi?

00:18:49.250 --> 00:18:52.340
Or what if he finds out
that Hiroki did it?

00:18:53.250 --> 00:18:55.590
Hiroki crushed Hayashi.

00:18:55.800 --> 00:18:58.720
He crushed him for going against
the idea of making "babies",

00:18:58.920 --> 00:19:00.550
then went on the run.

00:19:00.840 --> 00:19:02.850
What do you think Satoru would do?

00:19:03.180 --> 00:19:05.600
If he thought Hiroki had crushed Hayashi

00:19:05.810 --> 00:19:07.930
merely for opposing the idea
of creating "babies",

00:19:08.350 --> 00:19:11.940
of course he'd be more than willing
to change Hiroki's memories.

00:19:12.360 --> 00:19:13.810
Not bad, eh?

00:19:13.980 --> 00:19:17.530
The Company gets to tame both
Hiroki and Satoru in one move.

00:19:18.150 --> 00:19:21.740
This is my chance to crush Satoru.

00:19:29.080 --> 00:19:29.790
Hello?

00:19:30.040 --> 00:19:33.000
Well, who's a good boy then.
 You stayed in your room, I see.

00:19:33.210 --> 00:19:34.590
Yes, well...

00:19:35.000 --> 00:19:38.590
Let's have breakfast together again today.

00:19:44.720 --> 00:19:48.470
Don't worry.
Satoru doesn't suspect a thing.

00:19:48.680 --> 00:19:49.640
You're right...

00:19:49.930 --> 00:19:52.770
If things start feeling fishy,
just start speaking Chinese.

00:19:53.400 --> 00:19:56.360
That'll be my cue to come to your rescue.

00:19:59.280 --> 00:20:03.030
Erm, is Mr. Katsuragi not
 coming back today either?

00:20:03.570 --> 00:20:06.240
What's this?
You want him to come back soon?

00:20:06.410 --> 00:20:08.080
Course not!

00:20:09.410 --> 00:20:12.920
That's okay.
I'm not so fond of him myself.

00:20:13.120 --> 00:20:15.290
Since I was a child,

00:20:15.500 --> 00:20:17.750
I've always felt he lacked
the human touch.

00:20:17.960 --> 00:20:22.010
Oh yeah. I've been meaning to ask you
what Mr. Hayashi was like back then.

00:20:24.220 --> 00:20:29.100
Him and those other qigong masters
and the old guard crushers.

00:20:29.850 --> 00:20:34.400
I'd planned to tell you about Mr. Hayashi
and the original crushers today,

00:20:34.810 --> 00:20:36.900
so I brought a picture.

00:20:40.070 --> 00:20:42.450
Oh man... It's warm.

00:20:42.610 --> 00:20:46.280
Open it up.
Mr. Hayashi took the picture apparently.

00:20:48.200 --> 00:20:49.370
It's my mother.

00:20:50.410 --> 00:20:53.830
She was the very first of the crushers,

00:20:54.040 --> 00:20:55.290
and the CEO's younger sister.

00:20:56.130 --> 00:20:59.170
Oh, I see. You did say you were his niece.

00:20:59.590 --> 00:21:02.130
You see how she's laughing here?

00:21:02.340 --> 00:21:06.430
Apparently she'd never laughed
like that until Mr. Hayashi turned up.

00:21:08.760 --> 00:21:11.720
My mother had been emotionally unstable
since she was a child,

00:21:12.020 --> 00:21:14.310
so she was being cared for
by the qigong masters.

00:21:14.980 --> 00:21:19.320
But while they were looking after her,
one of the qigong masters got crushed.

00:21:19.940 --> 00:21:23.940
Because of that, my mother got given
the job of crushing people.

00:21:24.570 --> 00:21:28.950
After that, everyone was scared of mother
and didn't want to risk treating her.

00:21:29.370 --> 00:21:32.580
It was then that Mr. Hayashi turned up.

00:21:33.370 --> 00:21:36.790
He managed to calm my panicky mother
in no time at all.

00:21:37.290 --> 00:21:40.710
And he did it using a method none of
the qigong masters had ever seen.

00:21:41.340 --> 00:21:44.340
He synced up with her
to calm her down, didn't he!

00:21:44.760 --> 00:21:45.930
That's right.

00:21:46.130 --> 00:21:49.720
Thanks to him my mother was
able to marry, and then had me.

00:21:49.930 --> 00:21:51.640
She died young but...

00:21:52.390 --> 00:21:55.430
-her life was...
-But you have Mr. Hayashi!

00:21:56.520 --> 00:21:58.600
I mean, the other day...

00:21:58.810 --> 00:22:02.860
you said you wanted to enter the memory
of someone who knew your mom, right?

00:22:03.530 --> 00:22:06.360
I'm sure Mr. Hayashi would
let you sync up with him.

00:22:06.570 --> 00:22:08.360
You know, Satoru...

00:22:10.570 --> 00:22:12.620
Mr. Hayashi has returned.

00:22:14.580 --> 00:22:16.120
You serious? Where is he?

00:23:50.090 --> 00:23:55.010
"I got it... wrong?"
Artist: Ryo Ikuemi
